## Working with this codebase

These rules surface conventions enforced by the project's Rubocop/RSpec configs. Following them keeps CI green:

- Run `make codebase` before claiming a task is done. On Web, this also runs `yarn codebase` (ESLint + Stylelint). Use `make codebase/fix` for autofixes.
- Run the test suite via `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml run test` (executes `bin/test.sh` → `bundle exec rspec`).
- Use **Fabrication** (`Fabricate(:user)`), not FactoryBot. Fabricators live in `spec/fabricators/`.
- RSpec context wording: use `when` or `given` — `with`/`without` will fail Rubocop's `RSpec/ContextWording`.
- Line length is 130. Custom cops `CustomCops/ClassTemplate` and `CustomCops/RequiredInverseOfRelations` will fail CI if violated.
- Do not bypass git hooks with `--no-verify`.

## Common commands

- Start the dev server: `make dev`
- Lint: `make codebase` (autofix: `make codebase/fix`)
- Run all tests: `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml run test`
- Run a single spec inside the test container: `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml run test bundle exec rspec spec/path/to_spec.rb`
<%- if @install_openapi -%>
- Regenerate OpenAPI docs: `make doc/generate`
<%- end -%>
<%- if @install_phrase -%>
- Pull translations from Phrase: `bundle exec phrase pull` (push: `bundle exec phrase push`)
<%- end -%>
- Run migrations: `rails db:migrate` (or `make env/setup` for a fresh DB)
- Rails console: `docker compose run --rm web bundle exec rails console`

## Architecture notes

- Tests live under `spec/`; fabricators under `spec/fabricators/`; shared helpers under `spec/support/`.
- Rubocop config: `.rubocop.yml` at project root.
- Custom cops: `lib/custom_cops/` (shipped via the `custom_cops` template addon).
<%- if WEB_VARIANT -%>
- Frontend: Node 22 / Yarn. Asset entry points under `app/javascript/`. JS linting via `yarn codebase`.
<%- end -%>
<%- if API_VARIANT -%>
- JSON-only API — no views, no asset pipeline. Serializers live under `app/serializers/`. Use `render json: ...` and serializers, not view templates.
<%- end -%>

<%- if @install_devise -%>
## Authentication (Devise)

- User model: `app/models/user.rb`. Routes mounted under `/users` (sign-in, sign-out, etc.).
- Test helpers in `spec/support/devise.rb`. Use `sign_in user` in request/feature specs.
- Mailer views (password reset, confirmation) are in `app/views/devise/`.
<%- end -%>
<%- if @install_crud -%>
## CRUD scaffolding

- Generated CRUD controllers + views follow the Nimble CRUD addon convention: Slim views, Bootstrap 5 classes, scoped to the resource.
<%- end -%>
<%- if WEB_VARIANT && @install_bootstrap -%>
## Bootstrap

- SCSS entry point: `app/assets/stylesheets/application.scss`.
- JS entry point: `app/javascript/bootstrap.js`. Loaded via `app/javascript/application.js`.
<%- end -%>
<%- if WEB_VARIANT && @install_slim -%>
## Slim templates

- All views are `.slim`. Layouts under `app/views/layouts/`.
- The `html2slim` gem is available locally for converting ERB to Slim.
<%- end -%>
<%- if WEB_VARIANT && @install_hotwire -%>
## Hotwire

- Turbo + Stimulus are enabled. Stimulus controllers under `app/javascript/controllers/`.
- Turbo Frames/Streams are wired through `turbo_stream` partials in views.
<%- end -%>
<%- if @install_openapi -%>
## OpenAPI

- Spec lives under `docs/openapi/openapi.yml`. Regenerate with `make doc/generate`.
<%- end -%>
<%- if @install_nginx -%>
## Nginx

- Production reverse-proxy config: `config/nginx/app.conf.template.tt`.
- Used by the Heroku Nginx buildpack (see `app.json`).
<%- end -%>
<%- if @install_github_action -%>
## CI

- GitHub Actions workflows: `.github/workflows/`. Lint + tests run on every PR.
<%- end -%>

## Deploy

- Heroku is the deploy target. `app.json` configures review apps and production.
- `git push heroku main` deploys; CI must be green first.
